          "h": "",
          "p": "> Crowned the richest man at thirty, yet he stepped away swiftly at his very peak.\n>\n> Twenty years ago, mention his name and the entire Chinese-language internet — indeed all of China's business world — would give way. He was the chief of Shanda Interactive Entertainment: Chen Tianqiao.\n\nMaster Nao, in \"Ultimate Decoupling and the Life Strategy,\" said: the endpoint of wealth accumulation isn't the infinite collapse of numbers, but using absolute control to trade for absolute certainty and freedom of life.\n\n🔑 **1. Terror at the peak: the body becomes the most fragile liability**\n\nAround 2004, Chen Tianqiao held \"The Legend,\" a money-printing machine spitting cash daily, and Shanda was the toast of Nasdaq.\n\nYet he bore enormous public pressure. Countless parents cursed him as a peddler of \"electronic heroin\"; grand strategies like the Shanda Box were stuck at every step under the institutions and regulation of the time.\n\nIn extreme anxiety and high pressure, his body sounded the alarm — a severe panic disorder. On a plane he'd suddenly feel unable to breathe, his heart about to stop; he didn't even dare step into Shanda's office tower, breaking into a cold sweat at the mere approach.\n\nThis is the \"underlying resonance piercing\" at the financial and life levels: when the pressure a wealth system bears crosses the line, it directly backfires on the flesh.\n\nChen Tianqiao is extremely smart, and extremely reflective. He suddenly understood: if the physical \"1\" falls, all the \"0\"s behind — twenty billion, two hundred billion — mean nothing. Within the fierce competition of a single sovereign system, wealth brought no freedom, but became an invisible, inescapable cage.\n\n<center>✦ ✦ ✦</center>\n\n⚖️ **2. A total liquidation: the \"interstellar leap\" of clean cash**\n\nSeeing this, he showed a decisiveness rare among ordinary people. From 2009 to 2014, he did something remarkably clean: voluntarily delist, and sell off, in batches, all core assets — Shanda Games, Shanda Literature, and the rest.\n\nMany mainland bosses, facing crisis, can't let go of shares, thinking \"endure a bit longer,\" \"bet one more time.\" Chen Tianqiao doesn't bet. He chose to \"cash out\" the entire Shanda empire at peak valuation, when the market was most frenzied.\n\nThese post-tax, absolutely clean huge sums moved compliantly offshore, founding Shanda Group, an asset-management company. The allocation, too, revealed a top wealth-guardian's wisdom:\n\n- **US land, the hard-core constant.** He bought nearly 200,000 acres (about 800 square kilometers) of forest and land in Oregon and elsewhere. Land is the planet's oldest, most non-reproducible constant asset — no depreciation, no tech-iteration risk, eternally hedging inflation and geopolitical turbulence under the rigid protection of common law.\n- **All-in on brain science, boundless exploration.** He donated $1.15 billion to Caltech, seeking no commercial return, for one thing only: to figure out why the human brain feels pain and fear.\n\nThis completed his most thorough institutional switch: assets no longer depended on any single market's game licenses, on administrative approval, or on complex domestic human relations. He traded wealth from the high-volatility, high-pressure dividend track for the world's hardest land constant and the most detached scientific exploration.\n\n<center>✦ ✦ ✦</center>\n\n🌏 **3. Three-dimensional offshore: Chen Tianqiao's three epiphanies**\n\nTwenty years in the industry, I've met many mainland entrepreneurs in their forties and fifties. They resemble the Chen Tianqiao of those years, trapped in a \"sub-healthy, high-anxiety\" wealth trap.\n\nThey've earned tens or hundreds of millions, yet the business daily battles compliance checks, unpaid receivables, industry involution; they sleep on sleeping pills, their bodies long since flashing red. They feel they can never stop, always \"one more hundred million to be safe.\"\n\nChen Tianqiao, through a twenty-year life experiment, offers these guardians three awakenings:\n\n- **The ultimate premium of wealth is peace of mind.** Add a few more zeros to the books, yet if you still live daily in devaluation anxiety, policy panic, and physical pain, you're financially still a slave.\n- **Learn to \"draw down\" ambition.** Li Ka-shing taught us to rebalance in sunny times; Chen Tianqiao teaches us to exit at the peak. Don't wait until the industry rots, you're insolvent, your body collapses, to think of retirement. When the business is cleanest and most valuable, proactively turn some \"nominal assets\" into \"defensive constants\" — that is rationality of the highest dimension.\n- **True offshore is the three-dimensional unity of flesh, wealth, and spirit.** Opening an overseas account and buying a house abroad isn't true offshore. True offshore is letting assets stop anxiously tracking external swings, letting wealth serve what you truly love and what transcends the worldly, thereby gaining absolute freedom of flesh and spirit.\n\n<center>✦ ✦ ✦</center>\n\n💡 **4. In the noise, find that \"ultimate constant\"**\n\nChen Tianqiao's story is a wealth-redemption record of a Chinese richest man. With the most thorough resolve, he escaped the meat grinder of fame and fortune, and in forests and brain-science labs across the Pacific, found his family's eternal fulcrum.\n\nWe may not have his tens of billions, but every Chinese family that has lived through these recent cycles should light this awakening:\n\n- Moderately let go of the endless obsession with wealth \"high growth.\" In a low-rate, complex environment, stop blindly charging into high-risk entities or windfall projects.\n- Like his allocation of US land, allocate \"life redundancy\" where the rules are hardest. Through Hong Kong, the most convenient offshore window, turn a slice of existing wealth into offshore USD assets custodied by century-old multinational insurance giants, capturing global infrastructure and top-tech dividends.\n- Deeply bind wealth to the happiness of life. Let this constant wealth locked in Hong Kong become the confidence to say \"no\" to onshore involution at any time, the most solid physical safety net through health crises and industry storms."
