          "h": "",
          "p": "> He doesn't smoke, doesn't drink, has no illustrious background, and rarely appears in public.\n>\n> Yet this very person, under the extreme pressure of global geopolitics, carved out a near-miraculous path to survival for himself and his company. He is the soul of ByteDance — Zhang Yiming.\n\nMaster Nao, when explaining \"The Ultimate Manifestation of the Sovereign Individual,\" said something: the top elite of the new era no longer belong to any specific physical territory. Using algorithms, common law, and offshore nesting, they reshape themselves into a \"borderless sovereign individual.\"\n\n🔑 **1. Code rationality: the world's \"impossible trinity\"**\n\nMany mainland-going-global companies, when hit by an international political storm, are used to appealing to emotion, pulling connections, doing PR.\n\nZhang Yiming doesn't. In his underlying cognition, the world isn't composed of human feelings, but of an input-output system made of \"rules, law, jurisdiction, and physical boundaries.\"\n\nHe saw early a cold reality: a global tech giant grown from the mainland will inevitably crash into the global-geopolitics \"impossible trinity\" —"
