          "p": "Around 2020 the wind rose; some countries' executive orders aimed to surgically remove him, to force a divestiture. An ordinary person might resign to fate, exit, or fight to the death.\n\nZhang Yiming didn't. Like tuning a recommendation algorithm, he performed a years-long, millimeter-precise \"legal surgery\" on both ByteDance's and his own structure.\n\n<center>✦ ✦ ✦</center>\n\n🏛️ **2. Double hedging: ByteDance's two faces**\n\nHe upgraded \"asset decoupling\" and \"institutional heterogeneity\" from personal finance into an enterprise-grade global legal nesting. Three steps:\n\n- **Step one, cell division.** ByteDance split completely into two independent systems: Douyin rooted in the mainland, cooperating with local regulation, serving as the most stable cash-flow rear base; TikTok planted its headquarters in Singapore — the common-law center with the highest ethnic-Chinese ratio and the most neutral institutions — with data stored overseas and purely Western local executives. The two are physically, data-wise, and legally isolated; hit one, and you can't pierce the other.\n- **Step two, the offshore silence of the flesh.** After the split, in his thirties, he announced stepping down as CEO and quietly moved his life's center to Singapore. This echoes the core of Justin Sun's survival studies from installment eighteen — \"never place your physical self within the firing range of your wealth.\" Based in Singapore, his flesh is strongly protected by local law; any force wanting to apply pressure must go through lengthy, high-threshold international judicial process. He used offshore to buy back freedom of movement and rationality of decision.\n- **Step three, the equity trust's \"global nesting doll.\"** Not a single share of his personal stake is written under his own name; all is locked into multi-layer family trusts registered in Cayman and the BVI, with underlying assets custodied in a distributed way across the world's top banks.\n\nThe beauty of this structure: no matter how the storm tears, under the legal microscope, the outside world can find no single \"master switch\" that kills with one blow. Between two super-sovereigns, he built himself a damage-free \"rules buffer zone.\"\n\n<center>✦ ✦ ✦</center>\n\n🌏 **3. New money should have a globalist's big picture**\n\nIn twenty years in the trade, I've watched the mainland wealth class iterate from \"local tycoon boss\" to \"tech new-rich, cross-border elite.\" Many new-high-net-worth friends in their thirties, who made big money from the internet and going-global AI, carry Zhang Yiming's shadow: smart, efficient, international enough.\n\nA pity — many people's wealth-defense cognition still sits in the old era. They always feel \"I run a purely compliant business, not like Xu Jiayin with his high leverage, so I don't need to defend against anything.\"\n\nZhang Yiming, through his ordeal and breakthrough, taught the awake guardian the most stunning lesson:\n\n- **Compliance isn't a talisman; isolation is.** When macro volatility is violent, whether a person \"did something wrong\" often doesn't matter. Only by physically decoupling \"mainland career\" from \"offshore assets,\" like ByteDance splitting Douyin and TikTok, is the only solution.\n- **Singapore and Hong Kong are the Chinese ethnic group's natural firewall.** Zhang Yiming choosing Singapore was no accident. For ordinary high-net-worth families, these two Asian twin stars — Hong Kong and Singapore — are the hardest-ruled, closest common-law safe harbors.\n- **The highest realm of rationality is silence and redundancy.** True wealth isn't about being loud; it's, in sunny weather, quietly securing a second identity, opening an offshore account, and allocating large foreign-currency dividend assets. As installment seven put it: \"silent as water in calm times; when the black swan arrives, you're already seated on another ark.\"\n\n<center>✦ ✦ ✦</center>\n\n💡 **4. Like an engineer, code your family's risk-avoidance program**\n\nMost of us won't face Zhang Yiming's nation-level game. But the underlying algorithm of guarding is common to every high-net-worth family.\n\nIn this cycle of home-currency rate cuts and exchange-rate swings, take a page from the engineer and re-examine the family's asset structure:\n\n- Don't let the whole family's fate bet hard on a single basket. Carve out part of your clean funds and compliantly bring them to Hong Kong.\n- Using Hong Kong's common-law foundation, allocate USD-denominated, globally-arbitraged assets, such as large savings-dividend policies. Let the legal and actuarial teams of multinational insurance giants, at the base layer, complete for ordinary families the global quality-asset nesting that Li Ka-shing and Zhang Yiming achieved.\n- Set up an overseas account, or take a second identity, like Hong Kong's Quality Migrant or Top Talent schemes. Create for your family a \"life redundancy\" — switchable and cross-domain survivable at the critical moment."
