          "h": "2. The mainland annuity's curve",
          "p": "The mainland annuity's character is crystal clear: **extremely high certainty.** The pricing interest rate is written into the contract (currently capped at 3%), and you can calculate today the year-30 account value and annual payout. It's stable, but its ceiling is set by a single market's rate — in a rate-down cycle, that ceiling keeps dropping.\n\nFor those extremely averse to volatility who keep funds domestic, it's a qualified \"pension base.\""
