          "h": "5. Where does it fall short of a real trust?",
          "p": "Let's be clear: Hong Kong insurance's inheritance functions are powerful, but it's not a trust. A trust's asset-isolation scope is broader (real estate, equity can be loaded in), control finer (conditional distribution, staged payout). But a trust's threshold starts at several million USD, with annual maintenance easily hundreds of thousands.\n\nFor the vast majority of middle-class and newly wealthy families, **Hong Kong insurance's inheritance three-piece already covers 80% of inheritance needs**, with no setup fee, no annual fee, no lawyer team needed year-round.\n\n> A trust is a family heirloom, but not every family needs one. For most, a well-designed Hong Kong policy suffices."
